    "text": "To determine the age of Declan's younger son 30 years from now, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the current age of the elder son.\n2. Determine the current age of the younger son.\n3. Calculate the age of the younger son 30 years from now.\n\nStep 1: The current age of the elder son is given as 40 years.\n\nStep 2: The difference in age between the elder son and the younger son is 10 years. Therefore, the current age of the younger son is:\n\\[ 40 - 10 = 30 \\text{ years} \\]\n\nStep 3: To find the age of the younger son 30 years from now, we add 30 years to his current age:\n\\[ 30 + 30 = 60 \\text{ years} \\]\n\nThus, the age of the younger son 30 years from now will be \\(\\boxed{60}\\).",
